In this section, we learned how to use the PHP Dependency Injection (DI) container to manage the complexity of our applications by providing a single point of entry for all dependencies. We also learned about the Symfony Rate Limiter component and how to use it to limit the number of requests made to an external API. Finally, we discussed the benefits of using a dependency injection container in your PHP applications and provided some examples of real-world scenarios where it can be useful."]

