The `init_arrays` function is used to initialize the arrays with some dummy data. The `save_binary` and `save_text` functions are used to save the arrays to a file in binary and text format respectively. The `load_binary` and `load_text` functions are used to load the arrays from the file back into memory. Finally, the `print_arrays` function is used to print out the contents of the arrays.

Note that this code assumes that you have already implemented the `Record` struct and the `fwrite`, `fread`, `fprintf`, and `fscanf` functions in your program.']

