The function must handle potential memory allocation failures gracefully and ensure that no buffer overflows occur. Additionally, consider performance constraints and ensure that the function remains efficient even when handling a large number of log entries.

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <string.h>
